sed ECG abnormality (Tier-1 priority)", "Recent unregulated medication use"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Orthostatic/Postural Hypotension", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.20908660639330615, "posterior": 0.256979990446367, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Preserved supine blood pressure and no positional history argue against orthostatic hypotension as the fainting mechanism, but the LR+ of 1.6142 indicates only minor support, aligning with its current moderate elevation.", "Rapid neurological recovery weakly favors orthostatic/postural syncope over more dangerous arrhythmic causes, as brain injury is unlikely."], "evidence_against": ["The absence of orthostatic pressure changes with preserved baseline BP moderately supports alternative causes over orthostatic hypotension given the lack of positional syncope features in this patient’s presentation.", "Unknown positional BP data moderately reduces support for orthostatic hypotension (B1) despite environmental risk factors for volume depletion."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of positional changes leading to syncope", "Presence of postural symptoms in past medical history"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG for signs of sinoatrial node dysfunction", "Orthostatic blood pressure measurements"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cardiac Arrhythmia with Torsades-Des-Pointes Potential", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.16428233359474056, "posterior": 0.1560235656281514, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Rapid recovery makes torsades de pointes less likely, but the ECG remains the definitive test for this condition.", "No known CAD and lack of described ECG changes for STEMI argue against acute MI as the primary diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Medication history (including off-label use) linked to QT prolongation", "Witnessed arrhythmic features on this ECG"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG for QT interval and T-wave morphology", "Serum potassium and magnesium levels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Cardiac Ischemia (Acute/Previous)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.10422892361267055, "posterior": 0.08565999681545566, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["No known CAD and lack of described ECG changes for STEMI argue against acute MI as the primary diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B3.1", "B3.2", "B3.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Description of chest pain precipitating this episode"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Ischemic ECG changes (ST elevation/depression)", "Cardiac biomarkers (troponin)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Acute Vagal/Neurological Syncope with ECG Artifact", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.17131999363091133, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Ondansetron-Induced Torsades De Pointes", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.04588928400827982, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B2", "closu