ctural explanation for syncope.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.1": "strong_against"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented orthostatic BP measurements or positional history (despite hot weather exposure) moderate against orthostatic/postural hypotension as the primary mechanism for fainting?", "result_summary": "Unknown positional BP data moderately reduces support for orthostatic hypotension (B1) despite environmental risk factors for volume depletion.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "moderate_against"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the lack of hypokalemic ECG features (U-waves, flattened T-waves) and explicit mention of uncharacterised ECG findings provide strong evidence against ondansetron-induced torsades as the primary etiology?", "result_summary": "Uncharacterised ECG findings without hypokalemic patterns significantly reduce risk for drug-induced torsades (B2.1), which requires explicit QT interval and T-wave analysis to confirm.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B2.1": "strong_against"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Given no chest pain history and absence of Q-waves in ECG description, does this provide definitive evidence against prior myocardial infarction as the source of the current syncopal episode?", "result_summary": "While lacking chest pain history is suggestive, definitive evidence against prior MI (B3.1) requires explicit absence of Q-waves. Current findings only moderately support excluding MI.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B3.1": "moderate_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.30776349980422163, "B2": 0.205175666